; Regression test for issue #3243: an exact payee match outranks every
; other candidate.
;
; lookup_probable_account() gave an exact match a fixed score of 100 and
; stopped searching, but the more recent payees it had already scored
; stayed in the running, and the fuzzy score grows with the length of
; the identifier: "Nothing Bundt Cakes" scores 107 against "Nothing
; Bundt", so `xact "Nothing Bundt"` drafted from the Cakes transaction.
; In `convert --auto-match` those payees also outvoted the exact match
; when choosing the account: three visits to "Shell Beach Cafe" filed a
; "Shell" purchase under Expenses:Dining.  An exact match now outranks
; every merely similar payee and alone chooses the account.

2026-06-01 * Shell
    Expenses:Auto:Fuel                    40.00 USD
    Assets:Checking

2026-06-05 * Shell Beach Cafe
    Expenses:Dining                       20.00 USD
    Assets:Checking

2026-06-12 * Shell Beach Cafe
    Expenses:Dining                       22.00 USD
    Assets:Checking

2026-06-19 * Shell Beach Cafe
    Expenses:Dining                       18.00 USD
    Assets:Checking

2026-06-20 * Nothing Bundt
    Expenses:Takeout                       5.99 USD
    Assets:Checking

2026-06-25 * Nothing Bundt Cakes
    Expenses:Bakery                       31.87 USD
    Assets:Checking

test --now 2026/06/30 xact "Nothing Bundt"
2026/06/30 Nothing Bundt
    Expenses:Takeout                        5.99 USD
    Assets:Checking
end test

test --auto-match --account Assets:Checking convert $sourcepath/test/input/3243_exact.csv
2026/07/01 * Shell
    Expenses:Auto:Fuel                           -45
    Assets:Checking
end test
